{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778901153604,"sessionID":"ses_1d13b41dbffeaPo3a1GCslkylH","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-8cd0b8a765679b6a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json"},"output":"<path>/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\\n\\n*Parent term: MONDO:0700092 (Neurodevelopmental disorder)\\n\\nDefinition: This condition is associated with intellectual disability; growth delay; hypotonia; motor delay; ataxia; vision issues; cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy); and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia; cortical atrophy; and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension. \\n\\n**Definition source: PMIDs: 18711368, 20952379, 23562994, 32404165, 38347586, 38438125, and 38622473\\n\\n**Children terms: N/A\\n\\n**URL: https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [],\n4:   \"title\": \"New Term Request/TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\",\n5:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\"\n6: }\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\\n\\n*Parent term: MONDO:0700092 (Neurodevelopmental disorder)\\n\\nDefinition: This condition is associated with intellectual disability; growth delay; hypotonia; motor delay; ataxia; vision issues; cardiac features (including left ventricular hypertrophy); and pulmonary complications (such as acute respiratory distress and edema). It is also linked to brain structural anomalies such as pontine and cerebellar hypoplasia; cortical atrophy; and dilated ventricles. Renal features include proteinuria, thrombotic microangiopathy, end-stage kidney disease, and high-severity hypertension. \\n\\n**Definition source: PMIDs: 18711368, 20952379, 23562994, 32404165, 38347586, 38438125, and 38622473\\n\\n**Children terms: N/A\\n\\n**URL: https://clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40069/\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [],\n  \"title\": \"New Term Request/TSEN2-related neurodevelopmental disorder with or without thrombotic microangiopathy\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9956\"\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778901153594,"end":1778901153603}},"id":"prt_e2ec56c5a001xiB9cQN27qSwjN","sessionID":"ses_1d13b41dbffeaPo3a1GCslkylH","messageID":"msg_e2ec52b820017FxRxploQ9lqPg"}}
