e+W&cauthor_id=18711368), [Mohammad Reza Toliat](/?term=Toliat+MR&cauthor_id=18711368), [Yanick J Crow](/?term=Crow+YJ&cauthor_id=18711368), [Maja Steinling](/?term=Steinling+M&cauthor_id=18711368), [Thomas Voit](/?term=Voit+T&cauthor_id=18711368), [Filip Roelenso](/?term=Roelenso+F&cauthor_id=18711368), [Wim Brussel](/?term=Brussel+W&cauthor_id=18711368), [Knut Brockmann](/?term=Brockmann+K&cauthor_id=18711368), [Marten Kyllerman](/?term=Kyllerman+M&cauthor_id=18711368), [Eugen Boltshauser](/?term=Boltshauser+E&cauthor_id=18711368), [Gerhard Hammersen](/?term=Hammersen+G&cauthor_id=18711368), [Michèl Willemsen](/?term=Willemsen+M&cauthor_id=18711368), [Lina Basel-Vanagaite](/?term=Basel-Vanagaite+L&cauthor_id=18711368), [Ingeborg Krägeloh-Mann](/?term=Kr%C3%A4geloh-Mann+I&cauthor_id=18711368), [Linda S de Vries](/?term=de+Vries+LS&cauthor_id=18711368), [Laszlo Sztriha](/?term=Sztriha+L&cauthor_id=18711368), [Francesco Muntoni](/?term=Muntoni+F&cauthor_id=18711368), [Colin D Ferrie](/?term=Ferrie+CD&cauthor_id=18711368), [Roberta Battini](/?term=Battini+R&cauthor_id=18711368), [Raoul C M Hennekam](/?term=Hennekam+RC&cauthor_id=18711368), [Eugenio Grillo](/?term=Grillo+E&cauthor_id=18711368), [Frits A Beemer](/?term=Beemer+FA&cauthor_id=18711368), [Loes M E Stoets](/?term=Stoets+LM&cauthor_id=18711368), [Bernd Wollnik](/?term=Wollnik+B&cauthor_id=18711368), [Peter Nürnberg](/?term=N%C3%BCrnberg+P&cauthor_id=18711368), [Frank Baas](/?term=Baas+F&cauthor_id=18711368)\n\n### Affiliation\n\n-   1 Cologne Center for Genomics and Institute for Genetics, University of Cologne, Cologne, Germany.\n\n-   PMID: **18711368**\n-   DOI: [10.1038/ng.204](https://doi.org/10.1038/ng.204)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\nPontocerebellar hypoplasias (PCH) represent a group of neurodegenerative autosomal recessive disorders with prenatal onset, atrophy or hypoplasia of the cerebellum, hypoplasia of the ventral pons, microcephaly, variable neocortical atrophy and severe mental and motor impairments. In two subtypes, PCH2 and PCH4, we identified mutations in three of the four different subunits of the tRNA-splicing endonuclease complex. Our findings point to RNA processing as a new basic cellular impairment in neurological disorders.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## Publication types\n\n-   Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Research+Support%2C+Non-U.S.+Gov%27t%22%5Bpt%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Research+Support%2C+Non-U.S.+Gov%27t)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n\n## MeSH terms\n\n-   Brain / metabolism\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Brain%2Fmetabolism%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Brain)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Cerebellum / abnormalities\\*\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Cerebellum%2Fabnormalities%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Cerebellum)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Chromosome Mapping\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Chromosome+Mapping%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Chromosome+Mapping)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Chromosomes, Human, Pair 17\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Chromosomes%2C+Human%2C+Pair+17%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Chromosomes%2C+Human%2C+Pair+17)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Endoribonucleases / genetics\\*\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Endoribonucleases%2Fgenetics%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=d